$ABCD$ is a cyclic quadrilateral.
$\angle DAB = 108^{\circ}$.
Find $\angle BCD$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.902,0.618);
\coordinate (B) at (1.766,0.939);
\coordinate (C) at (-1.995,-0.14);
\coordinate (D) at (-0.877,-1.798);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\pic[draw, "$108^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.45cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = B--A--D};
\pic[draw, "$x$", angle radius=0.45cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = D--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$ABCD$ is a cyclic quadrilateral, and side $BC$ is extended to $E$.
